{"step_index":2002,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T13:56:09Z","input_tokens":3219,"cache_read_tokens":46827,"output_tokens":1149,"content":"Yes, exactly. **Xray acts as the SNI/domain-demuxing gateway, while Axum and Door 8090 handle the identity-aware pass-through.**\n\n---\n\n### How the Domain-Aware + Xray SID Flow Works\n\n```\n  Browser (sub.3tched.com)\n            │\n            ▼\n┌───────────────────────────────┐\n│     Xray Reverse Proxy        │  <-- Terminates TLS / Decoy SNI routing\n│  (Maps Domain -> SID1 Session)│  <-- Injects/authorizes the SID1 token\n└───────────┬───────────────────┘\n            │  Host: sub.3tched.com + x-identity: SID1...\n            ▼\n┌───────────────────────────────┐\n│    Axum Server (:8080)        │\n│  • Reads Host / SNI header    │  <-- Serves subsidiary-specific UI\n│  • DoorProxy connector        │  <-- Passes SID1 untouched to door\n└───────────┬───────────────────┘\n            │  gRPC-Web with SID1\n            ▼\n┌───────────────────────────────┐\n│       Door (:8090)            │  <-- Cryptographic admission\n│  • Verifies SID1 session      │  <-- Scopes D-Bus & memory calls\n│  • Enforces tenant boundaries │      to that subsidiary\n└───────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n1. **Xray** matches the incoming SNI / subdomain (e.g. `web3.3tched.com`), binds the request to the subsidiary's **SID1**, and forwards traffic to Axum on `:8080`.\n2. **Axum (`op-web`)** checks the `Host` / `X-Forwarded-Host` header:\n   * Serves the site-specific UI assets for that subsidiary.\n   * Its existing `door_proxy` forwards the untouched `SID1` credential straight to tonic Door `:8090`.\n3. **Door `:8090`** interceptor verifies the `SID1` and automatically scopes all D-Bus methods, vector queries, and memory loops to that subsidiary's identity.\n\n### Ready for the Post-12pm Identity Birth\n\nWhen you're ready after 12pm:\n1. We spin up the container in `/srv/git/3tched-container` with its private sparse device.\n2. Xray routes the subsidiary domain to that container's minted SID1.\n3. The new Web3 identity comes online with its own domain, private storage, and access to the shared holding cortex.","thinking":"The `door_proxy.rs` file details how gRPC-Web calls are proxied through `op-web` to the `tonic door`. Crucially, `op-web` does not handle the TLS certificate directly and simply forwards the calls; the door's interceptor performs identity verification. Xray's function is to manage incoming TLS termination, decoy routing, and SNI.\n\n\n"}
